            <ArticleTitle>Elevated high-density lipoprotein cholesterol, not protective in the presence of homocysteinemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>705-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Elevated high-density lipoprotein cholesterol is considered a protective factor for atherosclerosis. Very high density lipoprotein cholesterol is not necessarily protective in the setting of elevated plasma homocysteine concentrations.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
